module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.KrullDimension.Regular
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Intersection.ReductionToTheDiagonal.DiagonalRegularSequence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Intersection.ReductionToTheDiagonal.DiagonalStalkDimension

/-!
# The regular sequence cutting out the diagonal has length `dim X`

Let `X` be a nonsingular variety over a perfect field `k` and let `ξ` be a point of `X`. The
kernel of the map of local rings `𝒪_{X ×ₖ X, Δ(ξ)} ⟶ 𝒪_{X, ξ}` is generated by a regular
sequence (`Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap_diagonal`,
from Stacks tag 0B0Q), but that statement leaves the length of the sequence unspecified. This
file pins it down: the length is `dim X`.

The argument is the dimension count. For a regular sequence `rs` generating an ideal `I` of a
Noetherian local ring `B` one has `dim (B ⧸ I) + rs.length = dim B`, which is Mathlib's
`ringKrullDim_add_length_eq_ringKrullDim_of_isRegular` (Stacks tag 00KW iterated). Here
`B = 𝒪_{X ×ₖ X, Δ(ξ)}`, the ideal is the kernel of the local ring map of the diagonal, and that
map is surjective because the diagonal of a separated morphism is a closed immersion; so
`B ⧸ I ≅ 𝒪_{X, ξ} = A` and the formula reads `dim A + rs.length = dim B`. The dimension of `B`
is `dim X + dim A` by
`Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.ringKrullDim_stalk_pullback_diagonal`, so cancelling the finite
quantity `dim A` leaves `rs.length = dim X`.

The perfect-field hypothesis is inherited from Stacks tag 0B0Q and is not an obstruction here:
the chapter on intersection theory fixes an algebraically closed ground field, which is
perfect.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.length_eq_topologicalKrullDim_of_ker_stalkMap_diagonal` — any
  regular sequence generating the kernel of the local ring map of the diagonal at `Δ(ξ)` has
  length `dim X`.
* `Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.exists_isRegular_fin_generating_ker_stalkMap_diagonal` — the
  existence statement of Stacks tag 0B0Q with the sequence presented as a family indexed by
  `Fin c` for any natural number `c` equal to `dim X`. This is the form the reduction to the
  diagonal consumes, where the length of the sequence is the number `c` of generators of the
  ideal of the diagonal.

## Implementation notes

Both Krull dimensions in play are exhibited as natural numbers before the cancellation, rather
than cancelling in `WithBot ℕ∞` directly: the dimension of the variety is a natural number by
`Stacks.Intersection.exists_topologicalKrullDim_eq_natCast`, and the dimension of a Noetherian
local ring is one by Krull's height theorem, Mathlib's `FiniteRingKrullDim` instance for a
Noetherian local ring together with the nontriviality of a local ring. With both sides natural
numbers the cancellation is `omega`.

Noetherianness of the two local rings is not an instance that fires by itself: it comes from
`AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian` applied to the structure morphism
of `X`, respectively to `pullback.fst f f ≫ f` on the product, which is of finite type because
`f` is.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B0Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B0Q)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00KW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00KW)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal

/-- The Krull dimension of a Noetherian local ring is a natural number: it is finite by Krull's
height theorem and it is not `⊥` because a local ring is nontrivial. -/
theorem exists_ringKrullDim_eq_natCast (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] : ∃ n : ℕ, ringKrullDim R = (n : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have hnonneg : (0 : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ringKrullDim R :=
    (zero_le_ringKrullDim_iff_nontrivial (R := R)).mpr inferInstance
  have hbot : ringKrullDim R ≠ ⊥ := by
    intro h
    rw [h] at hnonneg
    simp at hnonneg
  cases hx : ringKrullDim R with
  | bot => exact (hbot hx).elim
  | coe x =>
    cases x with
    | top => exact (ringKrullDim_ne_top hx).elim
    | coe d => exact ⟨d, by simp⟩

/-- **The regular sequence cutting out the diagonal has length `dim X`.** Let `X` be a
nonsingular variety over a perfect field `k`, let `ξ` be a point of `X` and let `rs` be a
regular sequence of `𝒪_{X ×ₖ X, Δ(ξ)}` generating the kernel of the local ring map induced by
the diagonal. Then `rs` has length `dim X`.

Such a sequence exists by
`Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal.exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap_diagonal`; this is the
statement that its length is forced. Neither nonsingularity nor perfectness of `k` is used:
only that `X` is a variety, so that the two local rings are Noetherian and the dimension of `X`
is finite, and that the diagonal is a closed immersion, so that the local ring map is
surjective. -/
theorem length_eq_topologicalKrullDim_of_ker_stalkMap_diagonal {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsVariety k f] (ξ : X)
    {rs : List ((pullback f f).presheaf.stalk (pullback.diagonal f ξ))}
    (hrs : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular
      ((pullback f f).presheaf.stalk (pullback.diagonal f ξ)) rs)
    (hgen : Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker ((pullback.diagonal f).stalkMap ξ).hom) :
    (rs.length : WithBot ℕ∞) = topologicalKrullDim X := by
  have hlnX : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  have hftP : LocallyOfFiniteType (pullback.fst f f ≫ f) := inferInstance
  have hlnP : IsLocallyNoetherian (pullback f f) :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (pullback.fst f f ≫ f)
  -- the dimension drop along the regular sequence
  have hdrop := ringKrullDim_add_length_eq_ringKrullDim_of_isRegular rs hrs
  -- the quotient by the kernel is the local ring of `X` at `ξ`
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective ((pullback.diagonal f).stalkMap ξ).hom :=
    (pullback.diagonal f).stalkMap_surjective ξ
  have hquot : ringKrullDim
      ((pullback f f).presheaf.stalk (pullback.diagonal f ξ) ⧸ Ideal.ofList rs) =
      ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) := by
    rw [hgen]
    exact ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv
      (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hsurj)
  -- the dimension of the product at the point of the diagonal
  have hprod := ringKrullDim_stalk_pullback_diagonal f ξ
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := Stacks.Intersection.exists_topologicalKrullDim_eq_natCast f
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := exists_ringKrullDim_eq_natCast (X.presheaf.stalk ξ)
  rw [hquot, hm] at hdrop
  rw [hprod, hn, hm] at hdrop
  rw [hn]
  have : (m + rs.length : ℕ) = (n + m : ℕ) := by
    have h := hdrop
    push_cast at h
    exact_mod_cast h
  have hlen : rs.length = n := by omega
  rw [hlen]

/-- **Stacks 0B0Q at a point, with the length of the sequence pinned.** Let `X` be a nonsingular
variety over a perfect field `k` and `ξ` a point of `X`, and let `c` be a natural number equal
to `dim X`. Then the kernel of the map of local rings
`𝒪_{X ×ₖ X, Δ(ξ)} ⟶ 𝒪_{X, ξ}` is generated by a regular sequence of exactly `c` elements,
presented as a family indexed by `Fin c`.

This is the form the reduction to the diagonal consumes: the ideal of the diagonal is spanned
by the range of a regular family of `c = dim X` elements, so the multiplicity formula for a
regular sequence applies on the product with that `c`. -/
theorem exists_isRegular_fin_generating_ker_stalkMap_diagonal {k : Type u} [Field k]
    [PerfectField k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsVariety k f]
    (hX : IsRegular X) (ξ : X) {c : ℕ} (hc : topologicalKrullDim X = (c : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    ∃ g : Fin c → (pullback f f).presheaf.stalk (pullback.diagonal f ξ),
      RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular
        ((pullback f f).presheaf.stalk (pullback.diagonal f ξ)) (List.ofFn g) ∧
        Ideal.span (Set.range g) = RingHom.ker ((pullback.diagonal f).stalkMap ξ).hom := by
  obtain ⟨rs, hrs, hgen⟩ :=
    exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap_diagonal f hX ξ
  have hlen : rs.length = c := by
    have h := length_eq_topologicalKrullDim_of_ker_stalkMap_diagonal f ξ hrs hgen
    rw [hc] at h
    exact_mod_cast h
  refine ⟨fun i => rs[(i.cast hlen.symm : Fin rs.length)], ?_, ?_⟩
  · have hofFn : List.ofFn (fun i : Fin c => rs[(i.cast hlen.symm : Fin rs.length)]) = rs := by
      apply List.ext_getElem (by simp [hlen])
      intro i h1 h2
      simp
    rw [hofFn]
    exact hrs
  · rw [← hgen, Ideal.ofList]
    congr 1
    ext x
    simp only [Set.mem_range, Set.mem_ofPred_eq, List.mem_iff_getElem]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨i, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨i, by omega, rfl⟩
    · rintro ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨⟨i, by omega⟩, rfl⟩

end Stacks.Intersection.Diagonal

end
